# Badge states nothing can derive (.github#316): one line per shield that
# waits on a human step, or that names a registry coordinate the tree
# cannot infer. Everything else in the block is computed by fix:badges
# from this repository's own facts; lint:badges reddens a hand edit.
#
# crates: the crate whose version and docs stand for the family. edtf-core
# is the one every other member is built on, so its version is the family's.
# npm: the package name WITHOUT the scope; fix:badges adds
# @monumental-archive/ itself.
# bestpractices: edtf earned this before the transfer — project 13992, at
# Silver. The entry binds to a repository URL, so it is re-pointed rather
# than re-earned; the id does not change.
# reuse: registered 2026-11-14 at the org path. The pre-transfer
# registration named github.com/CarlAllenn/edtf, and api.reuse.software
# binds the badge to that URL, so the org path needed its own.
crates edtf-core
npm edtf-wasm
bestpractices 13992
reuse registered
